---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<BaseLayout title="About — Madhura Dharmadhikari" currentPage="about" headerVariant="about">
  <section class="about-content">
    <div class="about-line"></div>
    <div class="about-image-wrapper">
      <img
        src={`${base}images/placeholder/placeholder-2.jpg`}
        alt="Madhura Dharmadhikari"
        class="about-image"
      />
    </div>
    <div class="about-text">
      <p>
        Work explores Churchkill's relationship to female intimacy through the use
        of multiple art forms, shadows, and color.Churchkill's 'Mona' is part of
        Huxley Parlour's 'The Female Lens: 9 Contemporary Female Photographers' at
        the Photo London 2018 art fair. The body of work explores Churchkill's
        relationship to female intimacy through the use of multiple art forms,
        shadows, and color.
      </p>
      <p>
        The body of work explores Churchkill's relationship to female intimacy
        through the use of multiple art forms, shadows, and color.Churchkill's
        'Mona' is part of Huxley Parlour's 'The Female Lens: 9 Contemporary Female
        Photographers' at the Photo London 2018 art fair. The body of work explores
        Churchkill's relationship to female intimacy through the use of multiple art
        forms, shadows, and color. The body of work explores Churchkill's
        relationship to female intimacy through the use of multiple art forms,
        shadows, and color.
      </p>
      <p>
        My work combines Digital and Analog photography along with Mixed Media and
        stories to talk about what it is to live life with chronic conditions. My
        series have images as the base and depending on the project, it combines with
        materials and techniques that have held a unique place in my heart like
        painting, drawing and fibre art. My work is heavily inspired by my decade
        long experience of living with IgA vasculitis. The stories and incidents and
        the time I have spent by myself in recovery phases inspires me. Realising the
        lack of awareness and feeling the need to receive the right kind of support
        is what drives me.
      </p>
      <p>
        If talking about my experiences can benefit even one other person who
        experiences the same things as me, I would say that my suffering was not in
        vain.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-content {
    position: relative;
    padding: 0 177px;
    margin-top: 100px;
  }

  .about-line {
    position: absolute;
    left: 355px;
    top: 0;
    width: 2px;
    height: 1100px;
    background-color: var(--color-line);
    border-radius: 1px;
  }

  .about-image-wrapper {
    margin-left: 199px;
    margin-top: 33px;
    width: 687px;
    height: 1037px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .about-image {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .about-text {
    margin-left: 200px;
    margin-top: 30px;
    max-width: 687px;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--color-eerie-black);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .about-text p {
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .about-text p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
</style>
